```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: No operator needs the proposed agent-step-aware scheduler. Multi-agent LLM serving with interleaved tool-waits is already handled by vanilla continuous batching (vLLM/SGLang-style). The only actionable need is the negative guidance: do not invest in building a step-aware admission policy because the incumbent already captures the cross-agent bubble.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: No real win — microbenchmark (and even idealized slot-model) shows zero fillable idle. Residual_idle = 0.000000 across ALL 288 configs; CB decode-util equals the ready-work ceiling everywhere (packet L0 FINDINGS A). Paired step-aware vs CB at matched p99: median 0.00%, mean +0.32%, max +3.31%; TRUE wins = 7/288 all trivial (<1%, not concentrated at high rho); 0/288 beat CB non-trivially at matched p99; 66/288 “gain” only by sacrificing p99 (median 2.06× worse) (packet L0 FINDINGS B). The v1 “win” was a policy-dependent-RNG bug; v2 with byte-identical arrival tapes confirms CB==stepaware when M<B. The negative result is operationally meaningful as a kill signal, not as a product opportunity.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Incumbent CB already ships in vLLM/SGLang (Orca OSDI'22; PagedAttention SOSP'23) and strictly dominates the serial strawman (median 1.50×, max 7.99×) — packet L0 FINDINGS A; Step-aware adds per-agent burst tracking for zero median throughput gain; Any throughput delta requires unacceptable tail-latency tradeoff (p99 2.06× median, up to 3.5×); Real production bottleneck is KV-cache admission under correlated bursts, not slot occupancy — packet L0 LIMITATION notes “NO KV pressure, NO prefill. Any residual that exists is likely KV-BOUND not slot-bound.”]
RATIONALE: Packet L0 FINDINGS (A) “residual_idle = (ready-work ceiling - CB decode-util) = 0.000000 across ALL 288 configs. Vanilla continuous batching hits the ready-work ceiling EXACTLY everywhere — nothing to reclaim. The idle that exists is STRUCTURAL… no scheduler can decode work that isn't ready.” (B) “median 0.00%, mean +0.32%, max +3.31%; TRUE wins = 7/288 all trivial (<1%, NOT concentrated at high rho); 66/288 ‘gain’ only by SACRIFICING p99 (median 2.06x worse); 0/288 beat CB non-trivially at matched p99.” L0 LIMITATION: “occupancy model = 1 token/slot/step, fixed B, NO KV pressure, NO prefill. Any residual that exists is likely KV-BOUND not slot-bound.” Prior-art: “Continuous batching (Orca, OSDI'22; vLLM/PagedAttention, SOSP'23) is the obvious incumbent and it provably fills cross-request bubbles.”
```
